info.description:
- Endpoint: `GET /productv1/api.json` - websites selling products.
- Example: `https://api.builtwith.com/productv1/api.json?KEY=YOUR_KEY&QUERY=Adidas%20Yeezy`
- Credits: 1 per lookup.
- Pagination: response includes `is_more` and a `next_page` URL (`PAGE` and `LIMIT` parameters).

Sample response (`https://api.builtwith.com/samples/product_api_v1.json`):
```json
{
  "query": "Adidas Yeezy",
  "is_more": true,
  "next_page": "/productv1/api.json?KEY=[your-key]&QUERY=Adidas Yeezy&PAGE=1&LIMIT=50",
  "shops": [
    {
      "Domain": "example-shop.com",
      "Products": [
        {
          "Title": "Adidas Yeezy",
          "Url": "adidas-yeezy",
          "Price": 129.95
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Updated 2026-11-10 from https://api.builtwith.com/llms-full.txt. Set KEY locally. Requests are examples; sending data requests may consume credits. Optional query parameters are disabled until selected.
